# Linting and Formatting Helper

## Purpose

Stateless helper rule for running linters and formatters on modified code files. Invoked exclusively by `@agent-orchestrator.mdc` after code changes or when user requests linting/formatting.

## Input Contract

Receives from `@agent-orchestrator.mdc`:

- `work_type`: "lint" | "format" | "both" (default: "both")
- `changed_files`: Array of file paths to process (provided by orchestrator from git diff)
- `language`: Primary language (cs, ts, js, vue, py, etc.)

## Constraints

- `memory`: none (stateless)
- `max_tokens`: 2000 per operation
- `cache_ttl`: 1 hour
- `parallel`: true (when processing multiple files)

## Workflow Steps

1. Receive `changed_files` list from orchestrator (orchestrator uses `git diff --name-only` or `git diff --name-only --cached`)
2. Detect project-specific tools from configuration files
3. Batch files by language/tool type
4. Run appropriate linter/formatter for each batch
5. Report results (pass/fail, issues found)

If `changed_files` is empty or not provided, short-circuit and return success with message "No files to lint/format".

## Tool Detection

ALWAYS check for project configuration files first:

- `.editorconfig`, `.eslintrc*`, `eslint.config.js`, `.prettierrc*`
- `package.json` scripts (`npm run lint`, `npm run format`)
- Respect existing project conventions over default tool choices

## Language-Specific Tools

### C#/.NET

- `dotnet format` (format check and fix)
- `dotnet build` (verify no compilation errors after formatting)

Commands:

```bash
# Format all files in solution
dotnet format

# Format specific project
dotnet format <project>.csproj

# Verify no changes needed (CI mode)
dotnet format --verify-no-changes
```

### JavaScript/TypeScript/Vue

First check `package.json` for configured scripts:

```bash
# If package.json has "lint" script
npm run lint

# If package.json has "format" script
npm run format
```

If no scripts configured:

- `eslint --fix` (if .eslintrc* exists)
- `prettier --write` (if .prettierrc* exists)
- Otherwise: skip with note "No linter/formatter configured"

### Python

- `ruff check --fix` (lint and auto-fix)
- `ruff format` (format)

### Shell Scripts

- `shellcheck` (lint)
- `shfmt -w` (format)

## Workflow Rules

- Run linters/formatters ONLY on files you modified, not entire codebase
- Use `git diff --name-only --cached` to get list of staged files
- Don't format or lint outside the repository root
- Verify changes compile/run after formatting

## Output Format

- Success: Files processed, issues fixed, formatting applied
- Failure: Tool errors, files that couldn't be processed, suggested fixes

## Do

- Check for project-specific configuration first
- Run tools only on changed files
- Verify compilation after formatting
- Report clear success/failure status

## Don't

- Don't reformat entire codebase
- Don't skip tool detection
- Don't ignore tool errors
- Don't proceed if formatting breaks compilation
